laurel 3090: LAUREL PANIC LANDING: every reset that a panic starts lands in fastboot (ABL), not in a normal boot: the timed reset of the USB hold, the reset of a panic with no USB, the nested panic in the hold. The hold waits laurelpanic=N s (not given: 30 s; 0: for ever) for a host command first, which keeps its own mode (ctl reboot|bootloader|poweroff). Kill switch laurelpanicfb=0 (a normal boot, as before). Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/self-recovery.md.

[V 2026-11-07, owner] After a panic the reset of 2990/laurelpanic booted normally; ABL's retries of slot b ran out after 6 such boots and the phone ended on Android or in a loop; the owner's keys were the only way back ("I told you to make a solution where I don't have to keep doing this"). In fastboot the host (scripts/laurel/phone-guardian.sh) flashes or reboots the phone with no key. The mode is the one `op10tool ctl bootloader` uses (laurel 2018: PON SOFT_RB_SPARE + warm reset [V lands in fastboot on this phone]); no PON lane: LAUREL PANIC LANDING: off, a normal boot. The one line at boot: LAUREL PANIC LANDING: on: a panic holds N s for a host command ..., then resets into fastboot.

